// EXPECT-DIAG: Both branches of this 'if' do the same thing
// An if/else whose two bodies are the same is either redundant or a branch
// that was meant to differ. A lint warning, so the program still compiles and
// runs. NOTE the shape: the lint fingerprints only literals, variables and
// binary operations, so bodies made of assignments, calls or `return`s are
// never reported (see the Known thin spots in tests/CONFORMANCE.md) -- the
// case here is the one it can see, and nothing exercised even that before.
fn main(): int {
    mut a: int = 3;
    if a > 0 {
        a + 1;
    } else {
        a + 1;
    }
    return 0;
}
